Z||000000||turbo86se||08-02-2000||11:26 AM||||<BR>Now that I've got the 4-cyl out of my 88 coupe, I can see where all the rust is coming from! You should see my driveway!<BR>Everything from where the cat. convertor was (removed) all the way up to where the exhaust bolts to manifold including the clamps (flanges?) are rusted! Can I simply replace these pipes? <BR>I am installing a V6, so maybe the pipes are different? If so, anyone have any extra laying around? <BR>Thanks!!!||||reg||8
Z||000001||Megafiero||08-02-2000||01:51 PM||||Turbo86SE, the only real difference between a 4 banger and a V6 exhaust is just up by the motor,4 banger has strait pipe, V6 had a Y-pipe. A friend of mine put my old GT exhuast on his 84 with no problems.  If you can't find an exhaust system or if you decide you want a new one, check out <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierostore.com</A> <P>Megafiero<p>[This message has been edited by Megafiero (edited 08-02-2000).]||||reg||1
